Browser Use
Enable models to interact with web browsers to automate complex workflows and access real-time information.

Overview
Browser Use is a powerful capability that allows JLL GPT to directly interact with web browsers. Based on an open-source project and adapted for JLL GPT compatibility, this tool feeds screen contents from the browser to multimodal foundation models and uses LangChain's agentic AI components for reasoning and task completion.

This capability enables automated navigation, data extraction, and complex workflow execution across internal and external web applications.

How It Works
The Browser Use agent:

Captures and analyzes browser screen contents
Interprets visual information through multimodal AI models
Makes decisions based on content analysis
Executes browser interactions (clicking, typing, navigating)
Completes complex multi-step workflows autonomously
Example Use Cases
Example 1: Real Estate Data Extraction from Horizon
Task: Extract data about the largest Brookfield deal in Horizon, including the primary broker

Prompt Used:
Go to https://horizon.jll.com/
Sign in using SAML
In the search bar, type "Brookfield"
In the list of results, find what appears to be the largest deal by square feet
Open that deal
Find who the primary broker was on the deal
Result:
The agent successfully navigated to Horizon, authenticated, searched for Brookfield deals, identified the largest one (Brookfield Place at 8,400,000 square feet), and determined that Michael Shenot was the primary broker. Watch Demo Video

Example 2: Cross-Platform Property Listing Analysis
Task: Identify JLL properties not advertised on LoopNet and report via email

Prompt Used:
Go to https://property.jll.com/search?tenureTypes=rent&propertyTypes=office&orderBy=desc&searchInput=New%20York&sortBy=dateModified
Pick up the first 5 addresses of properties
For each property, search Google to see if the property exists on LoopNet. If it does, copy the link to LoopNet and continue. If it does not, remember this information for the next step
Go to https://outlook.office.com/mail/
Compose a new email with the subject line: "JLL properties not advertised on LoopNet", to: "or.hiltch@jll.com"
In the body of the email, write: "Dear Or, I have found some properties that appear to be marketed on the JLL leasing website, but are not advertised on LoopNet: {addresses of properties from the JLL website where no corresponding link was found on LoopNet}"
Result:
The agent successfully gathered property information from JLL.com, cross-referenced each property on LoopNet via Google search, identified missing listings, and composed an email report with the findings. Watch Demo Video

