The table is amazing, the only problem is that it's all made up. Despite claiming to have looked at every paper published in the Annals in this 75-year period, poking around the pages it looked at suggests it only looked at ~5-6 papers.

Frameworks and Design Patterns for Building Agents
Simplifying agentic systems
There are many frameworks that make agentic systems easier to implement, including:

LangGraph from LangChain
Scale AI
AI Squared
Xpander AI
Squid AI
Amazon Bedrock's AI Agent framework
Google's Vertex AI Agents Builder
Glean
Vellum, another GUI tool for building and testing complex workflows
Salesforces's Agentforce
ServiceNow's Moveworks AI
We have studied all of the above and more. These frameworks make it easy to get started by simplifying standard low-level tasks like calling LLMs, defining and parsing tools, and chaining calls together.

However, they often create extra layers of abstraction that can obscure the underlying prompts and responses, making them harder to debug. They can also make it tempting to add complexity when a simpler setup suffices.

We suggest that developers start by using LLM APIs directly with JLL GPT, or lightweight frameworks such as the OpenAI SDK. Many agentic patterns can be implemented in a few lines of code even without any framework. If you do use a framework, ensure you understand the underlying code. Incorrect assumptions about what's under the hood are a common source of customer error.

The OpenAI Agents SDK and JLL GPT
The OpenAI Agents SDK is a new, lightweight framework compared to LangGraph and LangChain that introduces useful abstractions for developing agentic AI apps, and can be easily used with JLL GPT API. It includes useful abstractions and many nice examples: voice agents, financial assistants, MCP and tools calling, etc. Everything on the API can interoperate with any third-party model provider, like JLL GPT API.

To quickly start building agents with the OpenAI Agents SDK, we have created a cloned and modified version that includes additional files to demonstrate JLL GPT integration.

