JLL LLM Gateway is an OpenAI-compatible proxy. Use this API to integrate with 100+ LLM providers (OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) through a single unified interface.

Overview

OpenAI-compatible endpoints: /chat/completions, /embeddings, /models, /completions, and more
Unified interface across multiple model providers
Base URL (UAT): https://api-ue1-am-apim-nonprod.jll.com/csp/aigateway
Base URL (Prod): https://api-llmgateway.jll.com
Authentication
All endpoints require both headers:

x-litellm-api-key: <your-api-key>
subscription-key: <your-subscription-key>
authorization: Bearer <your-okta-token>
Obtain your API key and subscription key from the LLM Gateway admin, and your Okta bearer token via your Okta session. Include all three headers in every request.

Error Handling
LiteLLM returns errors in OpenAI-compatible format:

{
  "error": {
    "message": "Error description",
    "type": "invalid_request_error",
    "code": "rate_limit_exceeded"
  }
}
Status Code	Meaning	Action
400	Bad Request – invalid parameters or model	Check request body and parameters
401	Unauthorized – missing or invalid API key	Verify your API key
403	Forbidden – valid key but insufficient permissions	Contact admin for access
404	Not Found – model or resource does not exist	Verify model name or endpoint
429	Too Many Requests – rate limit exceeded	Retry with exponential backoff
500	Internal Server Error	Retry once, then contact support
Rate Limiting
Requests are rate-limited per API key. When you receive HTTP 429, retry with exponential backoff.

